{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Send for yourself men.</b> Do not leave it to them to send, as they sought to do in saying נִשְׁלְחָה אֲנָשִׁים לְפָנֵינוּ (Deuteronomy 1:22) — lest they send commoners who do not recognize the excellence of the land, and who will speak ill of it, so that Israel will account HaShem as deceitful, and will not return in repentance as they did afterward in saying חָטָאנוּ לַה׳. For the scouts whom Moses sent, even though they sinned in turning the people's heart away through the deficiency of their faith in El Shaddai, nevertheless recognized and reported the goodness of the land, in saying וְגַם זָבַת חָלָב וּדְבַשׁ הִוא (Numbers 13:27), and likewise he testified in saying וַיִּקְחוּ בְיָדָם מִפְּרִי הָאָרֶץ, and they said טוֹבָה הָאָרֶץ (Deuteronomy 1:25) — only they said that conquering it would be impossible. And when Israel recognized their sin in not trusting in the salvation and victory of the exalted El, after He had done wonders among them, they returned in repentance and said חָטָאנוּ לַה׳, אֲנַחְנוּ נַעֲלֶה וְנִלְחַמְנוּ (Numbers 14:40), and they prayed, as he said וַתָּשֻׁבוּ וַתִּבְכּוּ לִפְנֵי ה׳ (Deuteronomy 1:45). Only the blessed El did not accept their prayer, because of the profanation of HaShem they had committed, which is not atoned except by death, as He testified concerning them in saying וּבְיוֹם פָּקְדִי וּפָקַדְתִּי וגו׳ (Exodus 32:34)." "<b>Every prince among them.</b> Whoever is the most distinguished in his tribe for recognizing the nature of the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:39.481759227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}